From 49c21c59906ef6295e01542e6a37deb12cdc2948 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:14:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gui: key-replace allows 15s, its press and waitFor went over
 5s under load

At load ~190, in a run of the key/provider/account GUI files, two of
this file's 420px cases went red with the element already there: the
double-click case's press on the key's field (resolved to the input,
then the action didn't finish in 5s) and zh-TW's waitFor of the row
the replace answer gives. Run again alone at load ~650, the file was
all green. The room is the file's own 5s default, as with
key-import.test.cjs (ce5b23cdb), not a rerun.

Run:
- key-replace.test.cjs, Chromium, all five languages, 1100 and 420,
  10 consecutive runs after the change, 40/40 each. Before it, the
  same file with an injected 6s stall on the field's Escape and a
  7s-late replace answer went red with the reported signatures
  (locator.press on elementHandle.press("Escape"), locator.waitFor on
  .acc[data-account-id="cccccccccc"]); with the room both pass under
  the injections.

Fixes #3476

Generated-by: GLM-5.3-Flash (ZCode)
---
 internal/gui/tests/key-replace.test.cjs | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/internal/gui/tests/key-replace.test.cjs b/internal/gui/tests/key-replace.test.cjs
index fa0107b8..c7cc346b 100644
--- a/internal/gui/tests/key-replace.test.cjs
+++ b/internal/gui/tests/key-replace.test.cjs
@@ -82,7 +82,9 @@ for (const engine of (process.env.BROWSER ? [process.env.BROWSER] : ["chromium",
         const browser = await (engine === "webkit" ? webkit.launch() : chromium.launch({ channel: "chromium" }));
         const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width, height: 800 }, reducedMotion: "reduce" });
         const page = await context.newPage();
-        page.setDefaultTimeout(5000);
+        // room for a busy machine: at load ~190 a press and a waitFor went
+        // over the 5s default with the element already there (#3476)
+        page.setDefaultTimeout(15000);
         const errors = [], posts = [];
         page.on("pageerror", (e) => errors.push(e.message));
         await page.route("**/*", serve(lang, posts));
